    "created_at": "2018-09-13T07:13:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-09-13T07:13:02Z",
    "body": "Thank you @annevk for adding a link, I wasn't aware this issue was already raised.\r\n\r\nIn #4026, @litherum and I agree that this should be in the visual order, and that advances are always from left to right (though there are cases where they are negative, such as combining marks.) It makes, however, knowing the advance of, say the 3rd character in the source text harder, because index of `advances` no longer matches to the index of the source text.\r\n\r\nAt this point, I don't know how to solve it, nor whether it is needed to be solved. I hope we can find solution if we learn the needs better, so I'm leaning to take the visual order for now, and keep listening to web authors what they want in addition. Opinion on this point is greatly appreciated.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
